# The macOS half of virglrenderer 1.3.0, applied by Vendor/build-virglrenderer.sh (patch -p1).
#
# vrend assumes a Linux OpenGL host. macOS's is 4.1 core over Metal: older, and stricter about
# what drivers elsewhere let through. Each hunk is one of those, found running a Linux guest on it:
#
# - Multisampling is probed, and allocated, only through glTex*StorageMultisample (GL 4.3). Without
#   it the probe reported 0 samples and the guest's Mesa offered no core profile at all; fall back
#   to glTexImage*Multisample (3.2), which macOS has.
# - A CLEAR_SURFACE naming a surface that does not exist failed the whole context. Mesa 25.2's virgl
#   sends exactly that (fixed in 25.3, which skips such a clear); drop it the way 25.3 would.
# - GLSL is written as #version 410 on macOS, leaving out #extension lines for what is core by 4.10:
#   macOS's compiler knows almost none of the ARB names and takes no #version 130.
# - Which vertex inputs are integers was only recorded on the vertex_attrib_binding (4.3) path, so on
#   4.1 an integer attribute met a float input and arrived as garbage (Skia's text vanished).
#   Recorded for every vertex element now. Takes effect with VIRGL_USE_INTEGER set.
diff -ruN a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c	2026-02-10 22:43:59
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c	2026-11-15 15:40:55
@@ -650,8 +650,10 @@
